UID:stanford_campus-localist-53741881207736-54299423855127@local-events
DESCRIPTION:The gut microbiome is a diverse colony of bacteria that reside
 s in each of us. Emerging research shows these bacteria play a key role in
  a healthy immune system. They are also associated with conditions such as
  obesity\, diabetes\, irritable bowel syndrome\, depression\, and a variet
 y of cancers. Yet most of us don’t know much about gut health or what to
  do to improve it.\n\nIn this noontime webinar\, you will be introduced to
  this secret world inside each of us through evidence-based research relat
 ed\n\nAges: All ages\nSource: https://healthyliving.stanford.edu/classes/r
