DESCRIPTION:Io's volcanism and Europa's surface bear witness to the dynami
 cs driven by tidal interactions of the Galilean moons with Jupiter. While 
 Europa and Ganymede host subsurface oceans\, which makes them prime candid
 ates for habitability\, tidal heating is unlikely to have been constant ov
 er the age of the Laplace resonance. In this talk I will revisit the coupl
 ed thermal–orbital evolution of the Galilean satellites using the astrom
 etric and geophysical constraints obtained over the past years. The Juno\n
 \nAges: All ages\nLast synced: 2026-11-18 13:08 PST
LOCATION:Mitchell Earth Sciences
END:VEVENT
